<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>We may collect the following information:</p>
<h3>2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Full name, company name, or organization name</li>
  <li>Phone number, email, and other contact details (e.g. LINE ID)</li>
  <li>Event details such as date, venue, event type, and special requirements</li>
  <li>Payment and receipt information (we do not store credit card details directly on our website)</li>
  <li>Messages or inquiries sent via contact forms, email, or social media</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 Information from Photo Booth Services</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Photos, videos, or audio recorded through our equipment at events</li>
  <li>Photo download data via QR Code or Cloud platform</li>
  <li>Data from AI Photobooth systems (e.g. AI-processed images)</li>
  <li>Messages or greetings recorded in Video Guestbook</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.3 Technical Information</h3>
<ul>
  <li>IP address, browser type, device, and operating system</li>
  <li>Website visit data, pages viewed, and time spent on the site</li>
  <li>Cookies and similar technologies (see Section 7)</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use personal data to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Provide photo booth rental services, equipment setup, and on-site operations</li>
  <li>Communicate, confirm bookings, send quotations, and coordinate before and after events</li>
  <li>Store and share photos/videos with event guests via QR Code or Cloud</li>
  <li>Design photo frames and customize services to your requirements</li>
  <li>Improve our website, analyze usage, and develop our services</li>
  <li>Comply with laws, regulations, and orders from relevant authorities</li>
  <li>Prevent fraud and maintain system security</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
<p>We process personal data on the following legal bases:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to provide services you book or request</li>
  <li><strong>Consent</strong> — e.g. newsletter subscription or photo/video capture at events</li>
  <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — e.g. improving services and system security</li>
  <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — e.g. retaining accounts and financial records</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Disclosure to Third Parties</h2>
<p>We may disclose information to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Our staff and service providers involved in our operations</li>
  <li>Cloud hosting providers, image storage systems, and website analytics tools</li>
  <li>Social media platforms you use to contact us (e.g. Facebook, LINE, Instagram)</li>
  <li>Government authorities when required by law</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not sell your personal data to third parties.
  For photos and videos at events, the event organizer may set additional usage policies,
  and we will act in accordance with our agreement with the organizer.
</p>

<h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
<p>
  We retain personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes stated in this Policy.
  In general:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Booking and contact data — as required by law or business necessity</li>
  <li>Photos and videos on Cloud — as specified in the contract or service package</li>
  <li>Technical data and cookies — as defined for each type</li>
</ul>
<p>
  When no longer needed, we will delete or anonymize the data
  unless law requires continued retention.
</p>

<h2>7. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
<p>
  Our website may use cookies to remember settings, analyze traffic,
  and improve your experience. You can configure your browser to reject cookies,
  but some features of the website may not work properly.
</p>

<h2>8. Data Security</h2>
<p>
  We use appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect personal data
  from unauthorized access, use, alteration, or disclosure.
  However, no system is 100% secure.
</p>

<h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
<p>Under the PDPA, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Access and request a copy of your personal data</li>
  <li>Request correction of inaccurate, incomplete, or outdated data</li>
  <li>Request deletion or destruction when no longer necessary</li>
  <li>Request restriction of processing in certain cases</li>
  <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
  <li>Object to processing in certain cases as provided by law</li>
</ul>
<p>
  To exercise your rights, please contact us at
  <a href="mailto:snapafoto@yahoo.com">snapafoto@yahoo.com</a>.
  We will respond within the timeframe required by law.
</p>

<h2>10. Children's Information</h2>
<p>
  Our services are often used at events with attendees of all ages.
  If children are photographed at an event, use of such images should have
  appropriate consent from parents or the event organizer.
</p>

<h2>11. Links to Other Websites</h2>
<p>
  Our website may contain links to third-party websites or services
  (e.g. Facebook, YouTube, LINE). We are not responsible for their privacy policies.
  Please read each website's policy before providing information.
</p>

<h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this Policy from time to time. Changes take effect when published on this page,
  with the latest update date shown above.
  For significant changes, we may notify you via our website or appropriate contact channels.
</p>

